From: INODE64 <ffelix@inode64.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:55:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Fix the "Timeout" sort option of apc.php

The "Timeout" entry of the user cache sort dropdown submitted SORT1=D,
so choosing it sorted by deletion time instead, and the option was never
shown as selected. Submit T, which the sorting code already handles.

Based on krakjoe/apcu commit 64b4a55 by Dennis Birkholz.
---
 apc.php | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/apc.php b/apc.php
index a514082..ec41380 100644
--- a/apc.php
+++ b/apc.php
@@ -936,7 +936,7 @@ EOB;
 		"<option value=C",$MYREQUEST['SORT1']=='C' ? " selected":"",">Created at</option>",
 		"<option value=D",$MYREQUEST['SORT1']=='D' ? " selected":"",">Deleted at</option>";
 	if($fieldname=='info') echo
-		"<option value=D",$MYREQUEST['SORT1']=='T' ? " selected":"",">Timeout</option>";
+		"<option value=T",$MYREQUEST['SORT1']=='T' ? " selected":"",">Timeout</option>";
 	echo
 		'</select>',
 		'<select name=SORT2>',
-- 
